2 contribution(s), 2 verified against the roster

NOT YET SATISFIED: no verified contribution comes from a participant declared independent of the operator. The security argument is that one participant destroyed a scalar without the others being able to compel or observe them; with every contribution inside one party's control that reduces to 'trust us', which is what the ceremony existed to avoid.
Reported rather than refused because --in-progress was passed. This is expected while the ceremony is still open, and it must be satisfied before the ceremony closes -- the final check is run without that flag.

